### Alta cerca de un incidente abierto (sustituye INCIDENT_ID por el que devuelva el 409)

### 1. Primera alta
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "FOREST_FIRE", "severity": 2, "latitude": 43.2265, "longitude": -4.3016 }

### 2. Otra alta a unos 500 m -> 409 Conflict con el incidente en "nearbyIncident"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "AVISO-2", "type": "FOREST_FIRE", "severity": 2, "latitude": 43.2310, "longitude": -4.3016 }

### 3a. Es otra emergencia: se confirma
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents?confirmNew=true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "AVISO-2", "type": "FOREST_FIRE", "severity": 2, "latitude": 43.2310, "longitude": -4.3016 }

### 3b. Es la misma: el aviso se añade al incidente (repetirlo no lo duplica)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/INCIDENT_ID/detections
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "AVISO-2", "latitude": 43.2310, "longitude": -4.3016 }
